  ('f4a1d442-873b-5453-9bec-ec8decf32157', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'self_development', 'O-3', 'active', 'Captain — Self-developmental', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Captains must complete DoD FM Certification Level 2. Captains should strive to obtain their CDFM and complete a graduate degree. FC captains should also seek additional FC functional training, including, but not limited to, Fiscal Law, PPBE, GFEBS Cost Management, Training with Industry, Joint Staff Fellowship Program, Congressional Fellowship Program, Intermediate Data Analytics Course (IDAC), GFEBS Intermediate Course, BOBJ and the Army Comptroller Course (ACC) to enhance professional development. In addition, FC captains can compete for ACS, TWI, internships, fellowships, and other broadening programs.', '0bfc943fec49d7e090b89d93dc60137ac474a1031844d4b3a480891796ae5544', 5, 5, '5', 16),
  ('a691f10f-300f-5d97-92c2-52c757f55834', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'rank_duties', 'O-3', 'active', 'Captain — Desired Experience', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Captains must attain basic technical and tactical skills in the application of FC core competencies and information systems, MDMP, Army doctrine (see Fig.2), and unit training management. Obtaining knowledge and experience in all FC core competencies as a captain is critical to personal and professional growth. Captains must gain a basic knowledge of U.S government operations, geopolitics, fiscal law, PPBE, force structure and characteristics.', 'feaaf6b63715581bb0cffb2a033e85bbf79dfe7a7e26addc78fbe7c512316229', 5, 5, '5', 17),
  ('54009c0d-05d9-502e-9ef5-bc6e99426bce', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'training', 'O-4', 'active', 'Major — Education', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Completion of ILE prior to the 13th year of commissioned service is critical to officer professional development and the foundation in preparing for KD assignments.', '6158f68fb0497698539d32f8f5a151be8de96f2719f1fc6ff9a23157bf8db5be', 5, 5, '5', 18),
  ('6ca80d42-30f5-5a9d-91ed-e952b2da3b2c', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-4', 'active', 'Major — Key Developmental Assignments', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Majors should serve in a KD position for 18 to 24 months.
