(b) ASA(FM&C) Staff Officer
(c) Chief of Staff
(d) War College Instructor
(e) Deputy Commander', '6f6d07e75467a5c3f84ead8d842f02c2d4c6f2186b24a941120d13bb8ad4c430', 11, 11, '11', 46),
  ('c3420abe-0f0c-5a9e-81f6-210ea6107417', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'self_development', 'O-4..O-6', 'reserve', 'Field Grade — Additional Training', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', 'Field grade officers must obtain and maintain their mandated DoD Financial Management program certification at Level III. Additionally, Field grade officers should obtain a professional credential; examples include CDFM, CGFM, CGAP, or CPFO. Reserve Component field grade officers should also seek additional Financial Management functional training to ensure they are well-rounded. See Figure 1 for recommended functional training. Reserve Component field grade officers should also possess a graduate degree from an accredited academic institution.', '492ca1741eaeab2d083bfcc5bbe9c884c6b8982770d4d2c2c9aba8171337022f', 11, 11, '11', 47),
  ('6fb9eada-cbab-5aa1-bf22-258d77b8ce8a', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'prerequisites', null, 'reserve', 'Branch Code 36A Requirements', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', 'Officers can request a branch transfer by completing the requirements listed below in section (1) and one or more requirements in sections (2) to (3):
(1) Officers who have completed an AOC or CCC in a different branch may satisfy branch code 36A by completing the following ATIS courses: Disbursing Operations Course, Accounts Payable Administration Course. Additionally, they must complete the following ATRRS courses: GFEBS Cost Management and Army PPBE.
(2) A minimum of 2 years in an FC assignment.
(3) Complete the Defense Comptrollership Program.', '542b2b56d62b1fa70d79f9de4f99a381ab1d9e06fab417b69473086ca1b66340', 11, 11, '11', 48),
  ('dfb0bc66-158f-5066-aac2-fb31a8699688', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'prerequisites', null, 'reserve', 'Branch Transfer for Army Reserve Officers', '5. Finance and Comptroller Reserve Component (RC) Officer Development', 'Reserve Component officers may transfer into the FC branch with the completion of Branch Code 36A requirements listed in section d.
(1) Submit the completed packet to the reserve unit admin section.
(2) The unit admin section must submit the request to FC Proponency for the Commandant’s review.
(3) FC Proponency returns the reviewed packet with the Commandant’s recommendation to the officer’s unit with concurrence or non concurrence for final submission to the Readiness Division (RD).', 'ce6ff903ef50ff5c2fa372c9f11ad058c8da4d50b7305337b9088e74fc864886', 11, 11, '11', 49),
  ('13297721-c9f7-50b9-88c8-8c49f6a3440c', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'development', null, 'guard', 'Officer Development', '6. Finance and Comptroller Army National Guard Officer Development', 'The ARNG officer Finance and Comptroller (FC) lifecycle development and utilization model (Fig 3) provides general guidelines on the assignments, training, knowledge, skills, and behaviors that contribute to a successful ARNG FC officer career. See the DA PAM 600-3 for additional guidance on ARNG officer development.', 'c8731cce115ceee4d81d83909f5b6e84a5e458e5360caa9afdd0e1a5bd82c55f', 14, 14, '14', 50),
  ('ce5a579d-e7be-5462-bf14-14e1160aec6f', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'training', 'O-1..O-3', 'guard', 'Company Grade — Education', '6. Finance and Comptroller Army National Guard Officer Development', 'The FC BOLC is the starting point for newly accessed FC officers. FC company grade officers should complete the resident BOLC by their second year of service. ARNG who have completed a BOLC other than the FC branch must complete the following ATIS classes, see (a) below, with a certificate of completion to satisfy the FC BOLC requirement. FC captains must complete either the resident FCCCC or the three-phase FCCCC–RC. This course includes one-distributed learning phase of nonresident instruction; and two active-duty training phases at the Finance and Comptroller School. Company grade officers who have completed CCC in a different branch must complete the following ATIS classes with certificates of completion to satisfy the FC CCC requirement: Disbursing Operations Course, the Accounts Payable Administration Course. Additionally, they must complete the following ATRRS courses: GFEBS Cost Management and Army PPBE.', '9eda0a6452fa0cad67604a012297b1e756637c984a27b166ac08422ab779bbaa', 14, 14, '14', 51),
  ('6e8e62d0-5456-5fad-b3b5-143b16189cb7', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'prerequisites', 'O-1..O-3', 'guard', 'Company Grade — ARNG Officers may have occupations or educational equivalent', '6. Finance and Comptroller Army National Guard Officer Development', 's that could also meet the requirements for branch transfers. Those officers, instead of the above (b. (1)) ATIS courses. should have one of the below to allow for branch transfer:
(a) A minimum of 2 years in an FC key development or utilization assignment or civilian/technician finance position equivalent to a 36A.
(b) Complete the Defense Comptrollership Program.', '1145a8e28768632acc349d06b909a7c1c947d142b5088304709858fa99d84942', 14, 14, '14', 52),
